  "details": "The username is being cut off in the new nameplate system as shown in the screenshots for reference with the live build.\n\nMaybe a possible solution could be adding a buffer of a few extra characters before it happens, to account for a bit longer usernames.\n\nBecause I also have a couple of people (who still play) in my friends list whos names are above the current character limit during account creation which is 15 characters,\n\nThose accounts are actual VRChat accounts and not the steam, google, discord or apple logins\n\nA buffer could also maybe take into account the bit longer usernames from for ex. steam accounts which add the extra 4 characters with a space at the end.\n\nThis was also a thing with the old old nameplates funny enough (2018 screenshot for some nostalgia).\n\nIt is not too big of a deal to me that it's cut off as it was also something in the far past in 2018 but its just something I've noticed,\n\nAs I do wish I could keep my username because I've had it since I started playing VRChat.",
